@startuml
!theme plain
title Contextual Bulk Upload and Immutable Versioning
actor "Authorised User" as User
participant "Unified Work Area" as UI
participant "Bulk Upload API" as API
participant "Permission Service" as Auth
database PostgreSQL as DB
collections MinIO as S3
queue "Extraction/Indexing (future worker)" as Worker
collections Qdrant as Vector

User -> UI: select multiple authorised files
UI -> API: files + metadata + scope + change reasons
API -> Auth: require content.bulk_upload in scope
Auth -> DB: active role assignment and scope lookup
Auth --> API: allowed
API -> DB: create upload batch
loop each file
  API -> DB: create upload item
  API -> DB: lock logical document (when revision)
  API -> DB: compare SHA-256
  alt exact duplicate
    API -> DB: mark duplicate and link existing version
  else new or changed content
    API -> S3: put object under tenant/document/version key
    S3 --> API: immutable storage VersionId
    API -> DB: create storage object + document version
    API -> DB: update logical current_version_id
    API -> DB: append audit and outbox events
    API -> Worker: enqueue extraction/indexing
    Worker -> Vector: upsert vector with mandatory tenant payload
  end
end
API -> DB: complete/partially complete batch
API --> UI: batch status and version records
@enduml
